ext/unicode/unidata.map is generated from these files of the Unicode 6.2.0 Character Database
(https://www.unicode.org/Public/6.2.0/ucd/): UnicodeData.txt, DerivedNormalizationProps.txt, SpecialCasing.txt and
EastAsianWidth.txt.

To regenerate it, from the repository root:

  ruby tools/mkunidata.rb UnicodeData.txt DerivedNormalizationProps.txt SpecialCasing.txt EastAsianWidth.txt > ext/unicode/unidata.map

Run against the 6.2.0 files, this reproduces the committed unidata.map byte for byte, and
spec/unidata_generator_spec.rb checks that it still does, using gzipped copies of the four files in
spec/fixtures/ucd-6.2.0/ (development-only; they aren't packaged in the gem). Moving to a newer Unicode version
changes the extension's output, and spec/ruby_parity_spec.rb pins the 6.2 behavior.
